# Declare a Prompt card

## Prerequisites

- py-wyrd installed and `WYRD_SERVER_URL` set
- A running server

## Recipe

```python
from wyrd.prompt import Prompt, PromptCard

# 1. Author the prompt spec
prompt = Prompt(
    name="summarise-document",
    version="0.1.0",
    template="Summarise the following document in {max_words} words or fewer:\n\n{document}",
    input_variables=["document", "max_words"],
)

# 2. Build the card
card = PromptCard(
    name="summarise-document",
    version="0.1.0",
    spec=prompt.to_spec(),
)

# 3. Optionally save locally
card.save()

# 4. Register
import wyrd
wyrd.cards.register(card)
```

## Notes

- Keep `name` stable — downstream agents, policies, and audits refer to it by
  identity.
- `version` follows semver. The server rejects a changed spec at the same
  version.
- `template` is the versioned content. Put operational rules in the spec rather
  than in free-form notes.

